<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Okmulgee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Okmulgee is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> Nation in 1867, after its removal from the South-East, and its sandstone Creek Council House of 1878 now serves as a museum. It remains the seat of the Muscogee Nation's government.</p></div>
